WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.406
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:04.676 --> 00:05.743
TOKYO-HAKONE EKIDEN RACE

3
00:05.810 --> 00:06.978
The Hakone Ekiden.

4
00:07.612 --> 00:12.350
Its official name is the Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race.

5
00:12.417 --> 00:17.288
Founded in 1920, it is the longest relay race

6
00:17.355 --> 00:19.257
in college long-distance running.

7
00:19.324 --> 00:23.628
Only 21 teams can compete.

8
00:23.695 --> 00:26.764
The top ten teams with automatic qualification,

9
00:26.831 --> 00:31.903
ten teams that clear the qualifying race, and the Kanto Student United Team.

10
00:32.837 --> 00:35.840
Each school passes down its uniform

11
00:35.907 --> 00:39.377
and the sash linking history and passion.

12
00:40.044 --> 00:43.948
As the new year dawns, a story unfolds of young runners,

13
00:44.716 --> 00:47.085
locked in a fierce battle, their souls throwing off sparks.

14
00:56.694 --> 01:00.965
BASED ON THE NOVEL ORETACHI NO HAKONE EKIDEN BY JUN IKEIDO

15
01:03.668 --> 01:05.470
KOKUSHIKAN UNIVERSITY TAKUSHOKU UNIVERSITY

16
01:10.875 --> 01:16.014
TOKYO-HAKONE ROUND-TRIP COLLEGE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

17
01:27.225 --> 01:29.761
Mr. Tokushige, less than one minute to air!

18
01:29.827 --> 01:31.129
I know!

19
01:33.665 --> 01:34.866
Thirty seconds to air!

20
01:36.267 --> 01:37.368
Made it!

21
01:37.902 --> 01:42.407
For Dainichi TV's Maradona, I've gotten pretty rusty.

22
01:42.473 --> 01:43.575
A hundred meters max.

23
01:43.641 --> 01:46.511
-Twenty seconds to air! -Bureau Chief Kitamura's been on my case.

24
01:46.578 --> 01:47.946
Video segment is cued.

25
01:48.012 --> 01:50.181
Nice shot on Camera One!

26
01:50.248 --> 01:51.416
-Mr. Tokushige. -Huh?

27
01:51.482 --> 01:54.352
-Please be quiet for a moment. -Okay.

28
01:54.419 --> 01:57.121
Opening video segment, Mr. Maeda, give us the opening call.

29
01:57.188 --> 02:00.258
Copy that. Opening video in 20 seconds. Thank you.

30
02:00.325 --> 02:02.227
-Ten seconds to air! -Okay.

31
02:02.293 --> 02:06.097
-Nine, eight, seven, six… -Here's the latest weather.

32
02:06.164 --> 02:10.835
-Five seconds! Four, three, two, one. -Roll the video segment!

33
02:10.902 --> 02:11.970
MIYAKO FOR HAKONE EKIDEN

34
02:16.708 --> 02:19.110
HAKONE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

35
02:20.044 --> 02:22.146
After the video segment, we'll open wide on the start.

36
02:22.213 --> 02:25.516
-Yes. -Close on the runners. Cameras, stand by.

37
02:25.583 --> 02:28.119
-Five seconds! -Four, three…

38
02:28.186 --> 02:30.521
‎-two, one. ‎-Camera one, go!

39
02:31.089 --> 02:31.889
At last,

40
02:31.956 --> 02:35.860
the time has come to fight for a spot in the Hakone Ekiden.

41
02:35.927 --> 02:37.095
For their school's honor

42
02:37.161 --> 02:39.564
and for their own futures,

43
02:39.631 --> 02:41.899
-a battle for every single second begins. -Go to the rules.

44
02:41.966 --> 02:44.435
Forty-two schools have entered.

45
02:44.502 --> 02:46.604
Each team can field up to 12 runners,

46
02:46.671 --> 02:47.905
and the top ten times determine

47
02:47.972 --> 02:49.641
-the standings. -Show the lineup graphic.

48
02:49.707 --> 02:52.844
Ten schools will earn a ticket to the main race.

49
02:58.983 --> 03:00.718
Let's go over the plan again.

50
03:00.785 --> 03:01.619
Yes, sir.

51
03:01.686 --> 03:02.654
MEISEI MANAGER - KEITO YANO

52
03:02.720 --> 03:05.290
Meisei, gather up! Strategy check!

53
03:05.356 --> 03:06.357
-Yes! -Yes!

54
03:08.693 --> 03:11.696
Yusuke and I will run in the lead pack and battle the other top runners.

55
03:11.763 --> 03:12.597
CAPTAIN - HAYATO AOBA

56
03:12.664 --> 03:15.500
The rest of you, form the second pack around Kengo!

57
03:15.566 --> 03:16.567
-Yes! -Yes!

58
03:16.634 --> 03:18.002
Everyone runs for everyone.

59
03:18.069 --> 03:20.705
Shave off every second you can.

60
03:21.472 --> 03:24.175
-Yusuke and I will lead the way. -Yes!

61
03:24.742 --> 03:27.312
All ten of us, under ten hours and 35 minutes total!

62
03:28.279 --> 03:29.314
Let's do this!

63
03:29.914 --> 03:30.782
-Yeah! -Yeah!

64
03:31.716 --> 03:32.583
Coach.

65
03:38.389 --> 03:41.459
You can do this.

66
03:42.827 --> 03:43.695
Got it?

67
03:44.662 --> 03:46.397
Go and seize Hakone!

68
03:46.464 --> 03:47.498
-Yes! -Yes!

69
03:48.599 --> 03:49.667
All right, huddle up!

70
03:53.304 --> 03:56.207
-Let's go! -Yeah!

71
03:57.241 --> 03:58.409
Keep Meisei on screen.

72
03:58.976 --> 04:00.745
This is their year.

73
04:00.812 --> 04:03.614
Leading Meisei Gakuin University is the legendary Coach Moroya.

74
04:03.681 --> 04:05.750
Close-up on the head coach. Okay, on-screen graphics.

75
04:05.817 --> 04:07.618
After heartbreak the last two years,

76
04:07.685 --> 04:09.520
they’re back at Hakone after three years.

77
04:10.088 --> 04:11.189
Commentator, Mr. Daigo.

78
04:11.255 --> 04:14.726
The once-fearsome coach looks calm today.

79
04:14.792 --> 04:16.227
Yes.

80
04:16.294 --> 04:19.097
If Meisei Gakuin's two top runners run to their ability,

81
04:19.163 --> 04:20.398
I think they could place high.

82
04:20.465 --> 04:21.666
-Mr. Hara. -Yes?

83
04:21.733 --> 04:22.600
The qualifying race

84
04:22.667 --> 04:25.370
has a different kind of tension.

85
04:25.436 --> 04:28.239
Because the ten runners' total time determines the result.

86
04:28.306 --> 04:30.041
One great runner isn't enough.

87
04:30.108 --> 04:32.710
-Every step matters. -Camera Two!

88
04:32.777 --> 04:37.148
You never know how a race will turn out until the very end.

89
04:37.782 --> 04:39.283
There's a monster lurking.

90
04:39.951 --> 04:40.885
Right.

91
04:40.952 --> 04:43.955
The pressure at the Hakone qualifying race is enormous.

92
04:44.021 --> 04:46.391
Anything can happen.

93
04:48.092 --> 04:50.762
A total of 504 runners

94
04:50.828 --> 04:53.965
now line up on the 45-meter-wide runway.

95
04:54.031 --> 04:56.467
The start is moments away.

96
05:00.071 --> 05:02.640
Thirty seconds to the start.

97
05:06.377 --> 05:07.211
Hayato.

98
05:10.281 --> 05:11.749
This is our last chance.

99
05:14.185 --> 05:15.153
We're going to Hakone.

100
05:15.219 --> 05:16.621
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

101
05:16.687 --> 05:17.688
Yeah.

102
05:20.391 --> 05:22.527
Ten seconds to the start!

103
05:23.060 --> 05:24.729
Camera Three, pan after the start.

104
05:24.796 --> 05:26.063
Then go to Car One.

105
05:26.130 --> 05:27.732
Come on.

106
05:28.299 --> 05:29.100
On your marks.

107
05:34.205 --> 05:36.007
And they're off!

108
05:36.808 --> 05:41.446
The fierce race for a place in Hakone has begun!

109
05:44.482 --> 05:46.083
Car One, go.

110
05:48.085 --> 05:49.587
After this, we go to the course intro.

111
05:49.654 --> 05:50.788
Copy that.

112
05:50.855 --> 05:53.057
Three, two,…

113
05:53.124 --> 05:55.426
one, start.

114
05:55.493 --> 05:59.297
The course is a half marathon. 21.0975 kilometers.

115
05:59.363 --> 06:02.133
Runners start at Japan Ground Self-Defense Force Camp Tachikawa

116
06:02.200 --> 06:03.768
and do about three laps of the runway.

117
06:04.302 --> 06:06.904
Then they head into town, and just before 14 kilometers,

118
06:06.971 --> 06:09.440
the stage shifts to Showa Kinen Park.

119
06:10.141 --> 06:14.579
Every year, one second can decide fate.

120
06:14.645 --> 06:16.781
That's the Hakone Ekiden qualifying race.

121
06:16.848 --> 06:19.951
Maeda's commentary really pulls it all together.

122
06:20.017 --> 06:22.053
Hakone is in good hands.

123
06:23.287 --> 06:26.257
The international runners have passed ten kilometers.

124
06:26.324 --> 06:29.260
At ten kilometers, a large Japanese pack is led by

125
06:29.327 --> 06:31.963
Meisei Gakuin's two top runners.

126
06:33.097 --> 06:36.033
The race has moved into Showa Kinen Park.

127
06:36.100 --> 06:39.904
And here comes Kenta Morimoto of Juntendo University!

128
06:44.809 --> 06:47.945
From the first pack, Kenta Morimoto of Juntendo…

129
06:48.012 --> 06:49.914
Hayato is looking good so far.

130
06:50.581 --> 06:52.717
At this rate, he'll beat the 1:03 target.

131
06:55.186 --> 06:56.053
Here they come.

132
06:56.621 --> 06:59.156
Come on, Hayato! Come on, Yusuke!

133
06:59.223 --> 07:00.958
Good pace!

134
07:01.025 --> 07:02.159
Come on!

135
07:05.563 --> 07:09.700
Hayato Aoba of Meisei Gakuin is running strong.

136
07:09.767 --> 07:13.004
Aoba missed the qualifying race

137
07:13.070 --> 07:14.906
the last two years because of injuries.

138
07:14.972 --> 07:17.508
He must be determined to make it count this time.

139
07:18.075 --> 07:19.944
-There's Meisei. I knew it. -Now Meisei's Aoba

140
07:20.011 --> 07:21.379
-Aoba. Caption. -draws level

141
07:21.445 --> 07:22.947
with Juntendo's Morimoto!

142
07:23.014 --> 07:23.848
You got it!

143
07:23.915 --> 07:26.117
Will Aoba make his move here?

144
07:29.787 --> 07:30.855
You got it!

145
07:32.590 --> 07:34.992
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY HAKONE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

146
07:45.937 --> 07:48.906
Oh, he's holding his side. Hayato Aoba of Meisei Gakuin

147
07:49.574 --> 07:51.008
-looks strained. -Is he okay?

148
07:51.075 --> 07:52.743
Stay on Aoba a little longer.

149
07:52.810 --> 07:56.113
Could that be a side stitch?

150
07:56.180 --> 07:57.748
It can happen when you're running well.

151
07:57.815 --> 07:59.150
Zoom out a little.

152
08:00.084 --> 08:02.720
Now Morimoto of Juntendo University moves back in front!

153
08:02.787 --> 08:03.654
KENTA MORIMOTO

154
08:04.655 --> 08:06.891
Will Juntendo University

155
08:06.958 --> 08:09.226
safely qualify?

156
08:09.293 --> 08:11.629
-Hayato! -Meisei Gakuin

157
08:11.696 --> 08:13.531
may have a problem.

158
08:14.031 --> 08:16.701
I'm worried about Captain Aoba.

159
08:20.271 --> 08:21.405
-Come on! -You can do it!

160
08:23.240 --> 08:24.609
-Come on! -You can do it!

161
08:24.675 --> 08:26.510
-Come on! -You can do it!

162
08:33.551 --> 08:36.120
Here is the turnaround at 17.4 kilometers.

163
08:36.187 --> 08:38.122
-Yusuke's on track for a personal best! -Mr. Daigo.

164
08:38.189 --> 08:41.392
What should runners watch for at this turnaround?

165
08:41.459 --> 08:43.027
We're already late in the race.

166
08:43.094 --> 08:45.763
Hayato is 20 seconds behind his target.

167
08:45.830 --> 08:48.032
And they also need to avoid…

168
08:49.634 --> 08:51.235
The runners behind…

169
08:51.302 --> 08:53.237
Hold that shot.

170
08:53.304 --> 08:55.072
-Showing on-screen graphics. -That's Shibata

171
08:55.139 --> 08:56.774
and Onishi of Nihon University.

172
08:56.841 --> 08:59.310
And three from Senshu University too!

173
08:59.377 --> 09:01.646
Everyone's making their move now!

174
09:01.712 --> 09:04.782
The final three kilometers are the hardest in a half marathon.

175
09:05.516 --> 09:08.219
Digging deep here will make all the difference!

176
09:08.285 --> 09:10.655
The schools are starting to make moves.

177
09:10.721 --> 09:11.689
Yes.

178
09:11.756 --> 09:13.891
-Hayato… -Meisei Gakuin's Hayato Aoba

179
09:13.958 --> 09:15.159
looks like he's struggling.

180
09:15.726 --> 09:17.762
Less than two kilometers remain.

181
09:17.828 --> 09:20.831
For a short stretch, there won't be any fans along the course.

182
09:28.906 --> 09:30.608
Yusuke and I will lead the way!

183
09:30.675 --> 09:31.842
We're going to Hakone.

184
09:31.909 --> 09:35.179
You can do this.

185
09:35.246 --> 09:36.947
Go and seize Hakone!

186
09:49.260 --> 09:51.462
Is Aoba picking up the pace again?

187
09:51.529 --> 09:52.863
Meisei Gakuin's Aoba…

188
09:52.930 --> 09:54.465
-Put up Meisei's caption. -Oh.

189
09:54.532 --> 09:56.067
He passes one runner here.

190
09:56.133 --> 09:58.903
-Center on Meisei and follow him. -He's giving everything he has

191
09:58.969 --> 10:01.105
to shave off one second.

192
10:06.143 --> 10:08.579
That's the captain's pride.

193
10:08.646 --> 10:10.181
-Captain Aoba -Hayato, you can do it!

194
10:10.247 --> 10:12.817
gives everything to this final push.

195
10:13.417 --> 10:16.520
Can Meisei Gakuin, the old powerhouse, make a comeback?

196
10:16.587 --> 10:18.255
Stay on Aoba's expression.

197
10:18.322 --> 10:20.491
He's giving it his all!

198
10:20.558 --> 10:21.692
Hayato Aoba!

199
10:39.243 --> 10:41.779
Runners are finishing one after another.

200
10:41.846 --> 10:44.415
They're shaving off every second they can!

201
10:44.482 --> 10:45.983
They're pumping their arms.

202
10:55.993 --> 10:59.430
Hakone is decided by the combined time of each team's top ten runners.

203
10:59.497 --> 11:00.731
Yusuke!

204
11:01.465 --> 11:03.901
-Great run! -Great run!

205
11:03.968 --> 11:05.603
-Great run! -Where is Hayato?

206
11:07.404 --> 11:08.773
We're in the closing stages.

207
11:08.839 --> 11:09.840
Hayato!

208
11:09.907 --> 11:11.509
He's giving

209
11:11.575 --> 11:12.743
it everything he has.

210
11:12.810 --> 11:13.644
-Let's go! -One second

211
11:13.711 --> 11:15.479
-You got it! -here could decide

212
11:15.546 --> 11:17.982
-whether they qualify for Hakone. -You got it!

213
11:21.051 --> 11:24.522
TOKYO-HAKONE ROUND-TRIP COLLEGE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

214
11:28.893 --> 11:30.027
Are you okay?

215
11:30.094 --> 11:31.996
-Can you stand? -Can you stand?

216
11:32.062 --> 11:33.664
-Let's move. -Yeah.

217
11:35.866 --> 11:38.769
NUMBER, NAME, GOAL TIME

218
11:39.470 --> 11:40.638
These schools have already…

219
11:40.704 --> 11:42.106
-How is it? -Yes.

220
11:42.173 --> 11:43.440
They've crossed the finish line.

221
11:43.507 --> 11:47.511
But this only means their top ten runners have finished.

222
11:47.578 --> 11:49.213
These are not the official standings.

223
11:49.713 --> 11:51.649
Great job, Hayato!

224
11:51.715 --> 11:52.583
My time?

225
11:55.119 --> 11:57.454
YUSUKE-ONE HOUR, TWO MINUTES, TEN SECONDS HAYATO-ONE HOUR, THREE MINUTES, 24 SECONDS

226
12:04.295 --> 12:05.629
It's okay, Hayato.

227
12:06.330 --> 12:08.833
Yusuke set a personal best and made up a lot of time.

228
12:11.068 --> 12:12.203
I'm sure we made it!

229
12:18.209 --> 12:21.412
The results will be announced shortly.

230
12:23.047 --> 12:26.817
The top ten schools from the last Hakone Ekiden are already seeded.

231
12:26.884 --> 12:29.687
They automatically qualify next year.

232
12:29.753 --> 12:32.623
Forty-two teams entered this qualifying race.

233
12:32.690 --> 12:35.960
Only ten will run the Hakone Ekiden.

234
12:36.527 --> 12:37.428
Will they make it?

235
12:43.367 --> 12:44.702
The results are coming up shortly.

236
12:44.768 --> 12:47.605
Stay on Meisei, Toho Economics and Senshu.

237
12:47.671 --> 12:49.940
Hakone Ekiden qualifying race…

238
12:50.007 --> 12:53.444
Only ten schools from this field will earn the right to run Hakone.

239
12:56.914 --> 12:59.383
TOKYO-HAKONE ROUND-TRIP COLLEGE EKIDEN QUALIFYING RACE

240
13:02.753 --> 13:06.123
We will now announce the results of the qualifying race

241
13:06.190 --> 13:10.194
for the Tokyo-Hakone Round-Trip College Ekiden Race.

242
13:11.228 --> 13:12.162
In first place…

243
13:12.229 --> 13:13.264
PLACE, UNIVERSITY, TIME

244
13:13.330 --> 13:14.632
Juntendo University,

245
13:14.698 --> 13:17.868
-10 hours, 33 minutes, 23 seconds. -Attention! Bow!

246
13:17.935 --> 13:19.270
Thank you!

247
13:19.837 --> 13:22.673
Second place is Nihon University…

248
13:22.740 --> 13:24.441
Take Nichidai.

249
13:24.508 --> 13:26.877
Nihon University takes second place.

250
13:28.679 --> 13:32.216
Sixth place, Nippon Sport Science University,

251
13:32.283 --> 13:35.552
10 hours, 36 minutes, 7 seconds.

252
13:36.120 --> 13:37.254
Seventh place,

253
13:38.889 --> 13:41.058
Yamanashi Gakuin University,

254
13:41.125 --> 13:43.894
10 hours, 37 minutes, 15 seconds.

255
13:43.961 --> 13:45.162
There's still a chance.

256
13:47.965 --> 13:51.735
Only three Hakone berths remain.

257
13:52.469 --> 13:55.306
Eighth place, Hosei University,

258
13:55.372 --> 13:57.341
-Okay, Hosei caption. -10 hours, 37 minutes.

259
13:57.408 --> 13:59.977
-It's Hosei University. Two remain. -21 seconds…

260
14:03.614 --> 14:04.715
Ninth place…

261
14:07.418 --> 14:10.287
Takushoku University, 10 hours, 37 minutes…

262
14:10.354 --> 14:13.057
-On-screen graphics for Takushoku. -Next is Takushoku University.

263
14:13.757 --> 14:15.960
Just one school left…

264
14:17.861 --> 14:19.129
Tenth place…

265
14:23.334 --> 14:26.303
Meisei… Meisei…

266
14:27.738 --> 14:28.939
The last school.

267
14:32.643 --> 14:35.379
Senshu University, 10 hours, 38 minutes, 2 seconds.

268
14:35.446 --> 14:37.281
-Take Senshu. -Senshu University claims

269
14:37.348 --> 14:40.017
the final Hakone berth.

270
14:40.584 --> 14:44.588
Those are the ten schools that qualify for the Hakone Ekiden.

271
14:49.560 --> 14:51.562
-Stay on Meisei and Toho Economics. -They'll run

272
14:51.628 --> 14:53.263
-Hakone next year. -Eleventh place…

273
14:54.999 --> 14:56.300
Meisei Gakuin University.

274
14:58.302 --> 15:00.771
Ten hours, 38 minutes, 12 seconds.

275
15:02.206 --> 15:04.208
By ten seconds.

276
15:04.274 --> 15:06.810
Unfortunately, Meisei Gakuin University

277
15:06.877 --> 15:09.980
failed to qualify for the Hakone Ekiden by ten seconds.

278
15:10.047 --> 15:12.616
They were only ten seconds behind Senshu University.

279
15:13.450 --> 15:17.021
-By ten seconds? -A world decided by just ten seconds.

280
15:17.588 --> 15:19.356
-The monster was there after all. -One second…

281
15:19.423 --> 15:20.858
Twelfth place…

282
15:23.627 --> 15:26.363
-Toho University of Economics. -Twelfth is Toho University of Economics.

283
15:33.771 --> 15:35.072
Hello, Tokushige speaking.

284
15:35.672 --> 15:38.042
Where are we on that thing?

285
15:40.277 --> 15:42.880
Could you give me a little more time?

286
15:43.614 --> 15:45.215
What are you talking about?

287
15:46.116 --> 15:48.452
We're less than three months from Hakone.

288
15:49.119 --> 15:50.220
You get that?

289
15:52.089 --> 15:52.956
Yes.

290
15:53.590 --> 15:57.061
Then let me talk to you next week.

291
15:57.127 --> 15:58.262
Goodbye.

292
16:13.744 --> 16:14.578
I'm sorry!

293
16:17.848 --> 16:19.016
I'm sorry, everyone.

294
16:20.517 --> 16:21.652
It's my fault.

295
16:25.823 --> 16:27.324
I'm sorry…

296
16:32.463 --> 16:34.264
Everyone, gather around.

297
16:41.939 --> 16:45.442
You gave it your best! You did really well!

298
16:48.612 --> 16:50.714
You guys gave it everything

299
16:51.348 --> 16:53.617
this entire year.

300
16:57.221 --> 16:58.255
But sadly,

301
16:59.723 --> 17:03.360
the dream didn't come true.

302
17:07.798 --> 17:11.502
You lost.

303
17:15.439 --> 17:16.507
But…

304
17:17.374 --> 17:20.577
it's great losers

305
17:21.612 --> 17:23.580
who make the winners shine.

306
17:26.617 --> 17:30.787
Right now, you are great losers.

307
17:31.955 --> 17:32.956
Starting tomorrow,

308
17:33.590 --> 17:39.296
run with the goal of becoming shining winners.

309
17:40.664 --> 17:42.332
Run with your heads held high.

310
17:43.467 --> 17:47.638
I'm proud of every one of you.

311
17:50.107 --> 17:51.475
Thank you.

312
17:55.946 --> 17:56.880
Hayato.

313
17:58.182 --> 18:00.784
Hold your head high and stand proud.

314
18:28.212 --> 18:29.646
SPORTS DEPARTMENT

315
18:31.481 --> 18:34.484
Five minutes for the qualifying race segment on the noon news?

316
18:34.551 --> 18:36.186
-Got it. -Mr. Tokushige.

317
18:36.920 --> 18:40.557
That qualifying race was something! Meisei Gakuin missed by just ten seconds!

318
18:41.091 --> 18:42.426
It gave me chills.

319
18:42.492 --> 18:45.662
-Races really are alive. -Right.

320
18:47.831 --> 18:49.399
-Um, excuse me. -Huh?

321
18:49.466 --> 18:52.603
I'm from a variety show called Laugh to Death.

322
18:52.669 --> 18:55.272
-I need clearance to use WBC footage… -Oh.

323
18:55.806 --> 18:57.374
For WBC, talk to him.

324
18:57.441 --> 18:59.409
-Mr. Muroi. -Yes.

325
18:59.476 --> 19:01.345
-Him. -Thank you!

326
19:02.012 --> 19:03.780
Don't make the players do anything too stupid!

327
19:04.381 --> 19:07.284
-Mr. Tokushige, the printout is ready. -Oh, thank you.

328
19:07.351 --> 19:10.387
HAKONE EKIDEN REFORM PROPOSAL

329
19:12.222 --> 19:13.423
HAKONE EKIDEN STAFF ROOM

330
19:13.490 --> 19:15.559
Wait, I have to watch all of these?!

331
19:15.626 --> 19:17.060
Show her how it works.

332
19:17.127 --> 19:18.428
Okay.

333
19:22.032 --> 19:23.300
Is it this one?

334
19:23.367 --> 19:24.334
CONTROL ROOM

335
19:24.401 --> 19:25.569
Okay.

336
19:25.636 --> 19:27.738
Zoom in on Car One in the back.

337
19:29.406 --> 19:33.277
You didn't understand Ms. Miyamoto's directions at the qualifier, did you?

338
19:34.111 --> 19:36.647
This includes the broadcast director's calls

339
19:36.713 --> 19:37.681
from the main race.

340
19:37.748 --> 19:39.549
It’ll help you understand the live workflow,

341
19:39.616 --> 19:40.851
so watch it and study up.

342
19:40.917 --> 19:43.654
Still, 20 years of this?

343
19:44.354 --> 19:46.123
That's 280 hours.

344
19:46.189 --> 19:47.658
Impossible!

345
19:47.724 --> 19:50.427
-Hey! -Good morning!

346
19:52.229 --> 19:53.797
-Oh, the Director's Voice. -Yes.

347
19:53.864 --> 19:56.066
I watched plenty of those.

348
19:56.133 --> 19:58.335
I recommend 2018.

349
19:58.402 --> 19:59.736
What happened that year?

350
19:59.803 --> 20:01.738
That's when Mr. Tokushige was the broadcast director.

351
20:02.873 --> 20:05.976
Cool, precise calls. Perfect flow.

352
20:06.043 --> 20:07.077
It'll give you chills.

353
20:07.144 --> 20:08.445
Right, Miyamoto?

354
20:08.512 --> 20:10.614
How long is the qualifying race segment for noon news?

355
20:11.581 --> 20:12.683
It's five minutes.

356
20:12.749 --> 20:15.786
Mr. Nomura, for five minutes, focus on the Juntendo captain's interview

357
20:15.852 --> 20:18.322
and Takushoku University's international runner.

358
20:18.388 --> 20:19.656
Got it.

359
20:19.723 --> 20:20.791
-Miyamoto. -Yes.

360
20:20.857 --> 20:21.892
Here.

361
20:22.726 --> 20:25.562
-Mr. Kuwa. Could you all take a look? -Huh?

362
20:25.629 --> 20:27.331
Everyone, take a look at this.

363
20:28.298 --> 20:30.133
"Hakone Ekiden Reform Proposal."

364
20:30.200 --> 20:32.169
I put it together myself.

365
20:33.003 --> 20:35.439
Looks good. More cameras too.

366
20:35.972 --> 20:36.907
It's realistic.

367
20:36.973 --> 20:39.676
Changes like these are totally fine,

368
20:39.743 --> 20:41.511
but will Bureau Chief Kuroishi accept this?

369
20:42.112 --> 20:44.081
Doesn't he want to turn Hakone into a variety show?

370
20:44.147 --> 20:46.149
Kuroishi?

371
20:46.216 --> 20:47.651
He's a tough opponent.

372
20:47.718 --> 20:50.487
He's Dainichi TV's very own…

373
20:50.554 --> 20:51.455
TETSU KUWANA

374
20:51.521 --> 20:53.423
What was it? That…

375
20:53.490 --> 20:57.027
-Like that pro wrestler. The De… -The Destroyer?

376
20:57.094 --> 20:59.763
-That's it. -Why do they call him that?

377
20:59.830 --> 21:02.666
He smashes precedent and sends the ratings soaring.

378
21:02.733 --> 21:04.634
That's the so-called Kuroishi Method

379
21:04.701 --> 21:06.603
that got him to Programming Bureau Chief.

380
21:06.670 --> 21:08.572
I heard he was the first to cast

381
21:08.638 --> 21:11.208
a comedian as an info show's main host.

382
21:11.274 --> 21:14.077
That was when I worked under him.

383
21:14.911 --> 21:17.614
I heard something the other day. They've started putting

384
21:17.681 --> 21:19.149
countdowns on kiss scenes in dramas.

385
21:20.117 --> 21:21.852
What, like "One minute to the kiss,

386
21:21.918 --> 21:23.754
59, 58…"? Like that?

387
21:23.820 --> 21:25.322
Wait, that's so convenient!

388
21:26.723 --> 21:30.427
Toyama, you totally watch dramas at double speed.

389
21:30.494 --> 21:31.828
-How'd you know? -Well,

390
21:31.895 --> 21:34.297
results are all that matter.

391
21:34.865 --> 21:37.134
Maybe countdowns will be normal someday.

392
21:38.201 --> 21:39.603
I'll upload the script when ready.

393
21:39.669 --> 21:40.570
Thank you.

394
21:40.637 --> 21:42.572
-I'll contact them properly later. -Okay.

395
21:43.373 --> 21:45.375
-Hashiguchi. -Yes?

396
21:45.442 --> 21:47.544
Okay. Let's go grab lunch.

397
21:48.512 --> 21:51.181
Mr. Tokushige, shouldn't you run

398
21:51.248 --> 21:52.983
the Hakone proposal by Bureau Chief Kitamura?

399
21:55.118 --> 21:57.287
He's been a weathervane lately.

400
21:57.354 --> 21:59.823
I'm Kitamura. Nice to meet you.

401
21:59.890 --> 22:02.793
Um… Needless to say,

402
22:02.859 --> 22:04.661
I'm against it.

403
22:05.462 --> 22:07.764
Doesn't Mr. Kuroishi just want credit

404
22:07.831 --> 22:09.933
for having changed something?

405
22:10.567 --> 22:12.803
I don't sense a shred of respect

406
22:12.869 --> 22:14.137
for sports broadcasting.

407
22:16.006 --> 22:18.208
Well, I'll talk to him.

408
22:19.109 --> 22:20.043
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

409
22:20.110 --> 22:21.044
TRACK AND FIELD TEAM DORMITORY

410
22:21.111 --> 22:22.712
HEAD COACH'S OFFICE

411
22:23.513 --> 22:24.581
Oh, come in.

412
22:27.484 --> 22:28.552
Excuse me.

413
22:32.756 --> 22:34.858
-Have a seat. -Okay.

414
22:46.002 --> 22:48.905
There's something I should tell you in advance.

415
22:51.541 --> 22:53.076
The truth is…

416
22:54.911 --> 22:57.814
I'm stepping down as head coach.

417
22:58.882 --> 22:59.716
‎Huh?

418
22:59.783 --> 23:02.085
I've done enough.

419
23:13.163 --> 23:14.364
I'm sorry…

420
23:19.302 --> 23:23.306
The qualifying race result is my fault.

421
23:25.809 --> 23:28.078
If I hadn't faded there,

422
23:30.247 --> 23:31.615
we'd surely have made the top ten…

423
23:32.782 --> 23:35.151
This isn't you guys' fault.

424
23:37.020 --> 23:41.391
I decided to step down a long time ago.

425
23:46.062 --> 23:50.534
For a long time, I've watched

426
23:50.600 --> 23:54.704
you guys more closely than anyone.

427
23:54.771 --> 23:56.273
That's why I know.

428
24:00.477 --> 24:01.811
You'll be fine.

429
24:02.879 --> 24:07.817
You can manage without me.

430
24:11.288 --> 24:16.126
From here on, I'll leave things to my successor.

431
24:18.895 --> 24:20.096
Your successor?

432
24:21.965 --> 24:23.767
It's already decided.

433
24:25.435 --> 24:26.836
Who is it?

434
24:28.605 --> 24:30.473
Masato Kai.

435
24:31.875 --> 24:32.742
Mr. Kai?

436
24:33.276 --> 24:35.278
-Masato Kai? -Yes.

437
24:35.345 --> 24:38.815
I heard it when I interviewed a Meisei Gakuin alum recently.

438
24:38.882 --> 24:41.818
Coach Moroya is retiring after this season,

439
24:41.885 --> 24:43.853
and Masato Kai will be the new head coach.

440
24:45.255 --> 24:47.524
What was his nickname again?

441
24:47.591 --> 24:49.726
-The "Meisei Express." -That's it.

442
24:49.793 --> 24:51.728
Was Mr. Kai really that fast?

443
24:51.795 --> 24:53.997
He ran the prestigious second leg from his first year.

444
24:54.064 --> 24:55.365
I think he's won the leg twice.

445
24:55.432 --> 24:57.701
He ran leg two all four years and won it three times.

446
24:58.635 --> 25:00.270
-Right. -Didn't he

447
25:00.337 --> 25:03.607
join a regular company after university?

448
25:03.673 --> 25:06.142
Yes, a big trading company, of all things. Uh…

449
25:06.209 --> 25:08.011
Tohto Chuo Bussan.

450
25:09.446 --> 25:11.281
Could you be quiet for a bit?

451
25:12.849 --> 25:15.719
Why would Mr. Kai suddenly come back?

452
25:16.853 --> 25:20.390
I heard he'd cut all ties with track.

453
25:21.691 --> 25:23.126
I see.

454
25:24.127 --> 25:27.163
So Kai's going to be a head coach…

455
25:27.230 --> 25:30.300
Is Mr. Kai quitting his company?

456
25:32.135 --> 25:36.206
He's taking a year's leave to come here.

457
25:37.173 --> 25:38.408
A year…

458
25:39.109 --> 25:43.113
Starting today, the team sets off

459
25:43.947 --> 25:46.650
with Kai for the next Hakone.

460
25:49.686 --> 25:51.988
And Hayato.

461
25:52.989 --> 25:55.825
You're on the Student United Team.

462
25:57.961 --> 26:00.563
The Kanto Student United Team

463
26:00.630 --> 26:03.800
is made up of the top 16 runners from teams that failed to qualify

464
26:03.867 --> 26:07.103
for the Hakone Ekiden.

465
26:07.170 --> 26:10.140
It participates as an additional 21st team.

466
26:10.707 --> 26:14.010
It's only open to runners who have never run the Hakone Ekiden.

467
26:14.077 --> 26:16.479
It is led by the head coach of the team

468
26:16.980 --> 26:19.916
that placed 11th

469
26:19.983 --> 26:21.484
in the qualifying race.

470
26:21.551 --> 26:23.520
Got it, Hayato?

471
26:25.455 --> 26:27.223
Earn one of the ten spots

472
26:28.058 --> 26:31.061
on the Student United Team.

473
26:32.028 --> 26:32.996
And run Hakone

474
26:33.863 --> 26:36.633
for the teammates

475
26:37.567 --> 26:39.169
who couldn't!

476
26:42.505 --> 26:46.943
So Mr. Moroya ends his career with the Student United Team?

477
26:47.010 --> 26:49.412
Apparently Mr. Kai will handle that too.

478
26:49.479 --> 26:51.047
He said there's no point.

479
26:51.614 --> 26:53.450
That's one unusual move after another.

480
26:54.017 --> 26:54.851
Um…

481
26:55.785 --> 26:57.654
I've always wondered about this.

482
26:57.721 --> 26:58.988
The Student United Team

483
26:59.055 --> 27:02.325
gathers top runners from schools that missed Hakone, right?

484
27:02.392 --> 27:04.294
So why do they never win?

485
27:04.360 --> 27:07.263
Other schools live and eat together 365 days a year.

486
27:07.330 --> 27:10.366
They come together as one.

487
27:10.433 --> 27:13.336
A team thrown together after the qualifying race can't beat that.

488
27:13.403 --> 27:15.238
And no matter how fast they run,

489
27:15.305 --> 27:17.774
their times don't go on record, right?

490
27:17.841 --> 27:19.642
They aren't ranked either.

491
27:19.709 --> 27:21.678
It's a non-scoring entry.

492
27:22.345 --> 27:26.716
So what motivates them to run?

493
27:28.918 --> 27:30.653
Because it's Hakone, maybe?

494
27:32.255 --> 27:33.590
Right.

495
27:34.591 --> 27:38.228
That's what Hakone is.

496
27:40.563 --> 27:42.398
As of today,

497
27:43.466 --> 27:46.536
I'm stepping down as head coach of this team.

498
27:46.603 --> 27:47.971
-Huh? -Huh?

499
27:48.037 --> 27:50.306
-Huh? -What? Resigning?

500
27:52.942 --> 27:56.246
For 38 years,

501
27:57.680 --> 28:01.184
I yelled at runners who didn't do as I wished

502
28:02.752 --> 28:05.255
and made them obey.

503
28:07.624 --> 28:09.726
I believed

504
28:11.261 --> 28:13.997
that was my way of coaching.

505
28:16.466 --> 28:17.300
But…

506
28:18.535 --> 28:20.937
it seems that was wrong.

507
28:21.738 --> 28:22.639
No.

508
28:24.707 --> 28:28.444
It was wrong.

509
28:29.746 --> 28:31.047
From here on,

510
28:32.148 --> 28:35.852
I'll entrust the team to a new head coach.

511
28:36.686 --> 28:39.556
-A new head coach? -A new head coach?

512
28:41.157 --> 28:42.625
Let me introduce him.

513
28:44.027 --> 28:45.762
Your new head coach, Masato Kai.

514
28:49.566 --> 28:52.569
NEW HEAD COACH OF MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY-MASATO KAI

515
29:02.812 --> 29:05.615
-A few words, please. -Sure.

516
29:10.386 --> 29:11.421
I'm Kai.

517
29:13.656 --> 29:15.491
We're going back to Hakone.

518
29:15.558 --> 29:18.094
That's my only goal.

519
29:19.596 --> 29:21.064
To get there,

520
29:22.031 --> 29:23.900
I'll overhaul the way things are done if needed.

521
29:24.400 --> 29:25.768
Overhaul?

522
29:29.939 --> 29:33.276
Be ready and follow me.

523
29:35.845 --> 29:36.679
That's all.

524
29:54.998 --> 29:56.633
Did you know about this?

525
29:59.869 --> 30:01.938
That Coach Moroya was quitting.

526
30:06.743 --> 30:08.044
I knew it.

527
30:11.381 --> 30:14.517
Do you really think Mr. Kai should be our head coach?

528
30:17.020 --> 30:17.854
What do you mean?

529
30:17.921 --> 30:20.456
He's using his company's social contribution program

530
30:20.523 --> 30:22.325
to coach us for only one year, right?

531
30:22.392 --> 30:23.559
So our team's being used

532
30:23.626 --> 30:26.729
to help his career.

533
30:28.364 --> 30:29.299
Who told you that?

534
30:29.365 --> 30:31.734
The Trustee, Ms. Yoneyama.

535
30:31.801 --> 30:33.870
The alumni association objects, too.

536
30:34.737 --> 30:38.007
The guys on our team say it's wrong too.

537
30:39.008 --> 30:41.010
Coach Moroya

538
30:41.077 --> 30:43.179
was tough, sure.

539
30:43.246 --> 30:45.915
But everyone looked up to him

540
30:45.982 --> 30:48.851
because we believed in him!

541
30:49.786 --> 30:52.055
Can we really make it to Hakone like this?

542
30:57.093 --> 31:00.129
Well, I guess it doesn't concern you.

543
31:02.598 --> 31:05.601
You're going to Hakone, right?

544
31:08.738 --> 31:10.473
With the Student United Team.

545
31:11.975 --> 31:13.443
He brought it up, didn't he?

546
31:14.911 --> 31:18.815
I ran Hakone in my first year, so I'm not eligible anymore.

547
31:20.850 --> 31:21.718
No.

548
31:23.252 --> 31:26.155
Nothing's official yet,

549
31:26.222 --> 31:27.190
-but… -But?

550
31:32.528 --> 31:33.696
Good for you, Hayato.

551
31:35.631 --> 31:37.567
Do your best for all of us.

552
31:37.633 --> 31:39.068
We'll all be cheering for you.

553
32:01.524 --> 32:02.759
Hayato!

554
32:06.062 --> 32:07.130
Thank you.

555
32:08.131 --> 32:09.832
Don't push yourself too hard.

556
32:13.369 --> 32:15.538
I can't settle down unless I'm doing something.

557
32:19.375 --> 32:23.246
Time will sort things out with Coach Kai.

558
32:24.247 --> 32:27.116
Everyone just hasn't come to terms with it yet.

559
32:35.191 --> 32:36.159
Um…

560
32:37.593 --> 32:40.263
I'm joining too, as team manager.

561
32:42.765 --> 32:44.033
The Student United Team.

562
32:46.069 --> 32:47.303
I'll do my best.

563
32:50.807 --> 32:51.674
I see…

564
32:59.282 --> 33:00.249
Hayato,

565
33:01.584 --> 33:06.022
are you having second thoughts? About running for the Student United Team?

566
33:11.461 --> 33:15.965
You missed the qualifying race the last two years because of injuries.

567
33:18.101 --> 33:22.171
I think I know how you felt

568
33:22.705 --> 33:24.540
watching Hakone these two years.

569
33:26.943 --> 33:30.480
That's why I want you to run.

570
33:38.621 --> 33:41.224
Should a captain who dragged the team down at the qualifying race

571
33:42.258 --> 33:45.928
be allowed to run Hakone?

572
33:51.934 --> 33:53.703
I was only ten seconds short.

573
34:02.645 --> 34:04.914
Oh, sorry.

574
34:05.681 --> 34:06.549
I'm going to bed.

575
34:07.817 --> 34:08.885
See you tomorrow.

576
34:17.159 --> 34:21.464
DAINICHI TV PROGRAMMING BUREAU CHIEF-TAKESHI KUROISHI

577
34:23.799 --> 34:25.334
HAKONE EKIDEN REFORM PROPOSAL

578
34:28.538 --> 34:32.275
As for Hakone,

579
34:32.341 --> 34:36.646
I don't intend to change the basic format.

580
34:36.712 --> 34:38.314
Think again.

581
34:40.716 --> 34:43.920
You think repeating the same thing will bring in more viewers?

582
34:45.154 --> 34:47.223
If you want better ratings,

583
34:47.290 --> 34:49.392
come up with a new framework.

584
34:49.458 --> 34:53.696
Which is why I'd add motorbike cameras

585
34:53.763 --> 34:56.032
to catch the tactics we've missed--

586
34:56.098 --> 34:57.266
Impact!

587
34:58.601 --> 35:01.137
Impact! Impact!

588
35:02.104 --> 35:03.206
Impact!

589
35:04.540 --> 35:08.211
What we need is impact like never before!

590
35:08.277 --> 35:10.546
Stop clinging to the old ways!

591
35:10.613 --> 35:12.982
-But-- -Those who don't care about sports…

592
35:13.049 --> 35:15.851
We need ideas that draw in people like viewers

593
35:15.918 --> 35:17.453
watching a comedy show instead.

594
35:18.554 --> 35:20.289
What exactly do you have in mind?

595
35:20.990 --> 35:22.925
Improve the studio guest lineup.

596
35:24.327 --> 35:26.529
-That's… -It's drab.

597
35:27.630 --> 35:28.798
Boring.

598
35:29.832 --> 35:33.502
That narrow view of sports coverage and all that talk about grit.

599
35:34.637 --> 35:37.840
Guests only Ekiden fans have heard of.

600
35:38.608 --> 35:40.376
It could use a star or two.

601
35:41.077 --> 35:45.014
Of course a show needs some glamour.

602
35:45.548 --> 35:49.118
But Hakone is a serious sports broadcast.

603
35:49.986 --> 35:53.723
We should avoid anything that drives away the true fans

604
35:53.789 --> 35:55.391
who've backed us for years, right?

605
35:58.227 --> 35:59.428
Tokushige.

606
36:01.364 --> 36:05.601
Don't you want to beat Kohaku in the ratings?

607
36:06.202 --> 36:07.570
Beat Kohaku?

608
36:13.976 --> 36:15.211
MR. HATAKEYAMA'S MANAGER-MORITA

609
36:15.278 --> 36:16.579
Hatakeyama…

610
36:17.280 --> 36:21.550
You mean the comedian Ippei Hatakeyama?

611
36:22.485 --> 36:24.787
Now that's impactful casting, right?

612
36:24.854 --> 36:26.722
I pried open his New Year's schedule.

613
36:26.789 --> 36:28.257
He even canceled his Hawaii trip.

614
36:29.425 --> 36:30.793
What do you mean?!

615
36:30.860 --> 36:33.362
He's popular with every generation,

616
36:33.429 --> 36:37.066
especially people in their 30s and 40s, who watch the most TV right now.

617
36:37.833 --> 36:39.035
I mentioned it to Mr. Tamuken.

618
36:39.101 --> 36:42.872
When I told him, he loved the idea. "The Hakone Ekiden? Great!"

619
36:43.873 --> 36:46.709
You already told President Tamura?!

620
36:49.645 --> 36:51.447
You can't be serious!

621
36:51.514 --> 36:53.549
I'm dead serious!

622
36:54.450 --> 36:57.820
Even you get it, right? This is Tamuken Pro.

623
36:57.887 --> 36:59.922
They practically run show business now.

624
36:59.989 --> 37:01.157
Why would you go and do that?

625
37:01.223 --> 37:04.560
You didn't move, so I moved for you.

626
37:04.627 --> 37:05.961
How about a thank you?

627
37:08.164 --> 37:11.233
Anything like this should go

628
37:11.300 --> 37:13.402
through my bureau chief first!

629
37:14.370 --> 37:17.573
You think I went over Kitamura's head?

630
37:18.974 --> 37:22.111
Mr. Kitamura approved it?

631
37:22.178 --> 37:23.679
Of course.

632
37:28.951 --> 37:32.254
Mr. Kuroishi, I'll say it again.

633
37:32.888 --> 37:35.424
That's not what the Hakone Ekiden is!

634
37:35.491 --> 37:37.626
Then what is it?

635
37:38.761 --> 37:40.463
So gathering Ekiden and marathon insiders

636
37:40.529 --> 37:43.432
to chat among themselves is serious?

637
37:44.033 --> 37:46.769
If a celebrity joins them, does that make it frivolous?

638
37:46.836 --> 37:50.172
That mindset is what makes it boring. Why don't you notice?

639
37:50.239 --> 37:53.409
Isn't it a stereotype to think

640
37:53.476 --> 37:54.944
celebrities guarantee ratings?

641
37:59.081 --> 38:00.716
You've got some nerve.

642
38:02.418 --> 38:07.289
The Hakone Ekiden needs observations grounded in experience

643
38:07.356 --> 38:10.393
and a deep understanding of the race.

644
38:10.459 --> 38:13.996
If we let amateurs with no race experience

645
38:14.063 --> 38:17.867
and questionable passion for sports comment,

646
38:17.933 --> 38:20.002
longtime Hakone fans

647
38:20.069 --> 38:22.071
will be completely turned off!

648
38:32.114 --> 38:35.017
Tokushige, listen.

649
38:36.318 --> 38:38.320
Between you and me,

650
38:40.022 --> 38:42.658
Mr. Kashiwagi agrees with me.

651
38:46.595 --> 38:48.130
The managing director?

652
38:51.200 --> 38:52.368
Good morning.

653
38:52.435 --> 38:54.804
DAINICHI TV MANAGING DIRECTOR MASAOMI KASHIWAGI

654
38:56.038 --> 38:57.473
So that's that.

655
38:58.874 --> 38:59.742
Got it?

656
39:13.322 --> 39:14.390
HATAKEYAMA'S IT'S SHOWTIME

657
39:14.457 --> 39:16.258
THURSDAYS AT 8 PM

658
39:20.663 --> 39:22.298
What's going on, Mr. Kitamura?

659
39:22.364 --> 39:23.499
About what?

660
39:23.566 --> 39:26.502
You heard about Mr. Hatakeyama, didn't you?

661
39:27.036 --> 39:28.671
Why didn't you tell me right away?

662
39:28.737 --> 39:31.841
Now that you mention it, he did say something.

663
39:31.907 --> 39:34.910
Why didn't you object when it first came up?

664
39:34.977 --> 39:35.878
Well,

665
39:36.412 --> 39:38.314
some trial and error isn't a bad thing.

666
39:38.380 --> 39:41.283
This is way beyond trial and error!

667
39:42.084 --> 39:43.786
You know what kind of broadcast

668
39:43.853 --> 39:46.188
the Hakone Ekiden is!

669
39:49.758 --> 39:50.893
Managing Director Kashiwagi?

670
39:52.261 --> 39:55.564
Are you going to bend our principles for sports broadcasting?

671
39:55.631 --> 39:56.932
I never said that.

672
39:56.999 --> 39:58.334
-You basically did. -When?

673
39:58.400 --> 40:00.035
It's the same thing.

674
40:02.004 --> 40:03.472
Listen, Tokushige.

675
40:04.206 --> 40:08.277
Think about office politics for once.

676
40:09.044 --> 40:11.313
Mr. Kashiwagi's probably the next president.

677
40:11.380 --> 40:13.148
Why go against him?

678
40:15.351 --> 40:17.753
Are we really putting a comedian on the Hakone broadcast?

679
40:17.820 --> 40:19.221
You're okay with that?

680
40:19.922 --> 40:22.057
Since when did our sports broadcasts

681
40:22.124 --> 40:23.526
-get so lightweight? -Shut up, Shige!

682
40:23.592 --> 40:25.594
I know that without you telling me!

683
40:26.262 --> 40:28.697
In this company, when Mr. Kashiwagi says yes,

684
40:28.764 --> 40:30.065
everyone below has to follow.

685
40:30.132 --> 40:33.002
-But that doesn't mean-- -I know what you want to say!

686
40:34.136 --> 40:37.406
So use that stubborn head of yours and figure it out!

687
40:37.473 --> 40:39.675
That's your job.

688
40:47.082 --> 40:49.418
My ears hurt.

689
40:51.787 --> 40:53.022
You're studying hard.

690
40:53.889 --> 40:55.791
Natsuki's pressuring me

691
40:55.858 --> 40:57.760
to watch it all by the end of the week.

692
40:57.826 --> 40:59.728
Isn't this workplace bullying?

693
41:00.596 --> 41:02.197
Hey, Tokushige!

694
41:02.765 --> 41:05.434
I said give me a wide shot of Tozai! Wide!

695
41:05.501 --> 41:06.635
That year,

696
41:06.702 --> 41:08.370
the weathervane was a broadcast director.

697
41:08.437 --> 41:10.105
I was the director in Car One.

698
41:10.172 --> 41:13.242
I'm talking to you, Shige! Answer me!

699
41:13.309 --> 41:16.111
That's scary! He's totally losing it!

700
41:16.745 --> 41:19.815
-I said look! -He was really scary back then.

701
41:20.382 --> 41:22.351
TEN YEARS AGO

702
41:22.418 --> 41:26.188
Shige, I told you to get his feet in the shot!

703
41:26.255 --> 41:27.856
I want his expression. Stay tight.

704
41:28.457 --> 41:30.693
-Please show a close-up. -Idiot!

705
41:30.759 --> 41:32.695
I said show his whole body!

706
41:32.761 --> 41:34.897
Hold it right there!

707
41:35.464 --> 41:37.833
You're the next broadcast director.

708
41:38.601 --> 41:39.868
I recommended you.

709
41:40.469 --> 41:41.604
Seriously?

710
41:42.338 --> 41:44.707
When you zoomed in on that runner's face,

711
41:45.708 --> 41:47.543
that worked too.

712
41:50.813 --> 41:51.814
I'm counting on you.

713
41:53.782 --> 41:54.850
Yes!

714
41:55.651 --> 41:57.419
-Ow! -Give it your best.

715
41:57.486 --> 41:59.054
-Give it your best. -That hurts!

716
41:59.888 --> 42:04.960
He probably didn't want to give up being broadcast director.

717
42:20.909 --> 42:23.912
THE HAKONE EKIDEN BROADCAST HANDBOOK NUMBERS 1-17

718
42:27.549 --> 42:28.617
NUMBERS 23-39

719
42:52.574 --> 42:56.211
It's a pleasure to meet you. I'm Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

720
42:56.278 --> 42:57.446
Sit.

721
42:58.580 --> 43:01.750
-Thank you. -Hello, I'm Tamura.

722
43:01.817 --> 43:03.719
I may not look it, but I'm busy.

723
43:03.786 --> 43:05.421
So nothing boring, okay?

724
43:08.090 --> 43:10.459
Please take good care of our Hatakeyama.

725
43:10.526 --> 43:12.094
He's all fired up.

726
43:12.628 --> 43:14.129
I think it'll make a great show.

727
43:15.931 --> 43:17.499
Honestly,

728
43:18.167 --> 43:21.670
I've hardly ever watched it. But my wife's

729
43:21.737 --> 43:24.006
a huge Hakone Ekiden fan.

730
43:24.073 --> 43:27.710
You know that hill past Yokohama? What's it called?

731
43:28.510 --> 43:30.312
Gontazaka? The toughest part of the second leg.

732
43:30.379 --> 43:31.947
That's the one!

733
43:32.014 --> 43:35.451
She made me buy a condo with a view of that hill.

734
43:35.517 --> 43:36.985
Just to watch the Ekiden!

735
43:37.786 --> 43:38.787
Jeez…

736
43:38.854 --> 43:41.590
At New Year's, she watches TV,

737
43:41.657 --> 43:45.160
then the hill, then TV, then the hill.

738
43:46.061 --> 43:47.563
She totally ignores me.

739
43:47.629 --> 43:53.135
So personally, I'm a little jealous of the Hakone Ekiden.

740
43:54.136 --> 43:57.439
Oh, and on clear days,

741
43:57.506 --> 43:59.908
you can see Dainichi TV in the distance.

742
44:00.442 --> 44:03.645
I might be spying on you with binoculars, so watch out.

743
44:09.885 --> 44:10.986
Thank you.

744
44:17.960 --> 44:20.362
Um, President Tamura.

745
44:21.263 --> 44:23.065
There's something I'd like you to hear.

746
44:24.233 --> 44:25.067
What?

747
44:26.235 --> 44:28.137
I'd like to tell you about 1987,

748
44:28.837 --> 44:33.142
when we first aired Hakone live.

749
44:34.710 --> 44:38.647
Back then, everyone said a live broadcast was impossible.

750
44:39.548 --> 44:43.886
The Hakone Mountains blocked the radio waves.

751
44:43.952 --> 44:45.420
They simply couldn't get through.

752
44:47.289 --> 44:52.261
After much thought, the staff decided to put relay equipment

753
44:52.795 --> 44:54.863
on the summit.

754
44:56.632 --> 44:58.433
Hauling dozens of kilos

755
44:58.500 --> 45:01.770
of equipment up trackless slopes

756
45:02.437 --> 45:04.206
was a matter of life and death.

757
45:05.307 --> 45:08.944
Why were they so set on a live broadcast?

758
45:10.112 --> 45:13.415
Because they wanted

759
45:14.283 --> 45:16.251
to capture the runners in the moment.

760
45:18.020 --> 45:21.657
The Hakone Ekiden is a race where the runners are the stars.

761
45:22.858 --> 45:28.430
Our job is to show the students as they are, in the moment,

762
45:29.531 --> 45:33.368
and to convey every nuance of the race thoroughly and accurately.

763
45:34.136 --> 45:40.075
So the staff and commentators stay in supporting roles.

764
45:41.076 --> 45:45.948
We simply show the runners and their race as it happens.

765
45:46.982 --> 45:51.420
That's why we've never invited

766
45:52.287 --> 45:54.256
a celebrity as a guest.

767
45:55.290 --> 45:57.025
"The more times change,

768
45:58.360 --> 46:01.630
the more valuable the unchanging Hakone Ekiden becomes."

769
46:02.564 --> 46:05.834
Those were the words of our first producer.

770
46:06.869 --> 46:10.739
With that resolve to never change,

771
46:11.506 --> 46:15.110
we've protected the broadcast every year.

772
46:17.279 --> 46:21.683
I don't know what you and Kuroishi discussed,

773
46:23.285 --> 46:27.723
but for now, we don't plan

774
46:28.957 --> 46:32.628
to have Mr. Hatakeyama on the Hakone Ekiden.

775
46:36.198 --> 46:38.967
I'm truly sorry.

776
46:44.773 --> 46:47.876
So you don't need Hatakeyama?

777
46:51.813 --> 46:53.682
Is Kuroishi saying that too?

778
46:54.616 --> 46:57.819
Kuroishi is the Programming Bureau Chief,

779
46:59.421 --> 47:03.725
but I'm fully responsible for producing Hakone.

780
47:03.792 --> 47:04.927
That's not what I'm asking!

781
47:07.663 --> 47:10.499
If you don't need our celebrities, fine.

782
47:11.733 --> 47:13.335
From now on,

783
47:13.402 --> 47:16.738
all Tamuken Pro celebrities will stay off Dainichi TV.

784
47:18.040 --> 47:19.374
Not just sports.

785
47:19.441 --> 47:22.844
Variety shows and dramas too.

786
47:23.979 --> 47:25.247
Sir, please wait…

787
47:25.314 --> 47:28.684
-Take the rest up with Kuroishi. -Sir!

788
47:36.425 --> 47:38.927
You damn idiot! Mr. Tamuken is furious!

789
47:39.528 --> 47:41.663
Go apologize now. Get on your knees if you have to!

790
47:43.966 --> 47:45.300
I'm sorry,

791
47:46.134 --> 47:50.906
but please let us broadcast the Hakone Ekiden as usual.

792
47:50.973 --> 47:54.109
You're going against Managing Director Kashiwagi's wishes?

793
47:55.210 --> 47:57.079
I'd follow him if he were right.

794
47:58.180 --> 47:59.581
But he's not.

795
48:00.649 --> 48:01.883
Listen.

796
48:01.950 --> 48:05.354
The Hakone Ekiden doesn't belong to you!

797
48:06.288 --> 48:08.290
It doesn't belong to the Sports Department either.

798
48:09.024 --> 48:12.661
It's Dainichi TV's precious asset!

799
48:14.029 --> 48:15.731
Don't forget that.

800
48:19.835 --> 48:20.736
Mr. Kuroishi.

801
48:21.269 --> 48:22.371
What?

802
48:23.939 --> 48:30.345
The Hakone Ekiden doesn't belong to me or to Sports Department.

803
48:31.546 --> 48:32.447
And…

804
48:34.249 --> 48:36.218
it doesn't belong to Dainichi TV.

805
48:41.189 --> 48:42.824
It belongs to the runners.

806
48:47.195 --> 48:49.464
You've got some nerve.

807
48:51.600 --> 48:53.168
Listen carefully, Tokushige.

808
48:54.936 --> 48:57.139
You've got two choices.

809
48:58.673 --> 49:03.011
Get on your knees to Mr. Tamuken and have Hatakeyama on Hakone,

810
49:03.712 --> 49:06.381
or take the blame for losing

811
49:06.448 --> 49:10.152
all Tamuken Pro celebrities from Dainichi TV.

812
49:10.218 --> 49:12.821
I want your decision

813
49:12.888 --> 49:15.557
by the executive meeting early next week.

814
49:18.860 --> 49:22.898
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY TRACK AND FIELD TEAM

815
49:51.493 --> 49:54.696
From now on, we'll meet as a group twice a month.

816
49:54.763 --> 49:58.733
You'll set goals at the start of the month and check your progress.

817
49:58.800 --> 50:01.603
Then think about what you need to do

818
50:01.670 --> 50:02.971
to reach them.

819
50:03.972 --> 50:06.108
Each of you, set goals for your running

820
50:06.174 --> 50:09.478
that are as specific as possible.

821
50:10.278 --> 50:12.747
That's it for practice today.

822
50:12.814 --> 50:14.716
-Good work. -Um…

823
50:17.686 --> 50:19.621
You told each of us to set

824
50:19.688 --> 50:21.356
specific goals.

825
50:22.591 --> 50:23.692
But before that,

826
50:24.626 --> 50:27.395
could you tell us your coaching philosophy?

827
50:29.197 --> 50:32.501
What I just said is my coaching philosophy.

828
50:41.309 --> 50:43.111
-Mr. Nomura, did you hear? -Huh?

829
50:43.178 --> 50:45.981
A Tamuken Pro actor might suddenly drop out,

830
50:46.047 --> 50:48.750
so the January drama can't start shooting.

831
50:50.285 --> 50:51.553
Oh, really?

832
50:51.620 --> 50:54.389
Next week's Hatakeyama's It's Showtime

833
50:54.456 --> 50:55.757
taping got postponed too.

834
50:55.824 --> 50:58.193
What? I was scheduled to shoot that.

835
50:58.260 --> 51:00.295
My location shoot today got canceled

836
51:00.362 --> 51:02.130
because the Tamuken celebrity can't come.

837
51:02.197 --> 51:04.099
It was my first variety gig in ages.

838
51:04.966 --> 51:07.636
Mr. Tokushige really did it this time.

839
51:09.838 --> 51:12.541
Mr. Yasuhara, whose side are you on?

840
51:12.607 --> 51:16.044
Huh? It's not about sides.

841
51:16.111 --> 51:19.447
Is this Mr. Tokushige's fault?

842
51:22.384 --> 51:23.852
Right.

843
51:23.919 --> 51:26.421
The real problem is Kuroishi

844
51:26.488 --> 51:28.890
pushing ahead and ignoring the crew.

845
51:28.957 --> 51:30.659
Totally. I bet he just sees Hakone

846
51:30.725 --> 51:33.295
as popular content.

847
51:33.361 --> 51:35.964
I want Mr. Tokushige to really fight back too.

848
51:37.465 --> 51:40.302
-Good morning. -Good morning.

849
51:58.119 --> 51:58.987
What's up?

850
52:00.622 --> 52:03.825
Well, I guess I know what's up.

851
52:05.860 --> 52:06.828
Is it okay?

852
52:07.629 --> 52:08.463
‎Yeah.

853
52:08.997 --> 52:13.201
I've been on an apology tour around the building all morning.

854
52:15.570 --> 52:16.671
But it's okay.

855
52:17.539 --> 52:19.140
I'll figure something out.

856
52:20.242 --> 52:23.245
Don't worry. Just keep working.

857
52:23.912 --> 52:25.880
-Okay. -Okay.

858
52:27.549 --> 52:30.986
Though I guess you can't help worrying.

859
52:36.758 --> 52:37.826
Hold on!

860
52:40.729 --> 52:42.664
What do you mean, "frivolous"?!

861
52:44.466 --> 52:47.302
How are we frivolous?!

862
52:48.970 --> 52:50.505
Say something!

863
52:54.175 --> 52:56.578
We've got trouble! There's a fight!

864
52:56.645 --> 52:58.613
-Who? -Natsuki.

865
52:58.680 --> 52:59.714
Ms. Miyamoto?

866
52:59.781 --> 53:02.284
She's arguing downstairs with a variety director from her year.

867
53:02.350 --> 53:03.685
Variety?

868
53:03.752 --> 53:05.687
A Tamuken Pro pop idol might quit their show.

869
53:05.754 --> 53:07.956
They were glaring at each other.

870
53:08.023 --> 53:09.557
It was all "Take responsibility!"

871
53:21.236 --> 53:23.071
Um, Mr. Tokushige.

872
53:25.974 --> 53:30.679
Maybe we could reconsider having Mr. Hatakeyama on after all.

873
53:32.180 --> 53:35.350
Of course, we'd get creative with how he appears,

874
53:35.984 --> 53:39.421
as long as we protect the way Hakone's always been broadcast.

875
53:44.759 --> 53:45.660
Um…

876
53:46.961 --> 53:49.531
-I think so too. -Toyama.

877
53:50.565 --> 53:52.067
I mean, why not, right?

878
53:52.133 --> 53:54.369
People who want to see Mr. Hatakeyama

879
53:54.436 --> 53:56.538
might come to love Hakone because of this.

880
53:57.439 --> 53:59.574
Giving viewers what they want to see

881
53:59.641 --> 54:01.609
is part of our job too.

882
54:03.011 --> 54:04.045
Is it?

883
54:06.915 --> 54:08.583
"Giving them what they want to see"

884
54:09.117 --> 54:12.821
just sounds like pandering to me.

885
54:13.888 --> 54:15.824
Isn't giving viewers something

886
54:15.890 --> 54:19.160
that moves them for a lifetime

887
54:20.295 --> 54:22.364
worth far more than a fleeting number?

888
54:26.468 --> 54:28.103
I'm against

889
54:28.169 --> 54:31.272
bringing frivolous variety stuff

890
54:32.407 --> 54:33.975
into sports broadcasting.

891
54:38.413 --> 54:39.447
Miyamoto.

892
54:40.682 --> 54:43.685
Have you ever really watched a variety show?

893
54:45.587 --> 54:46.554
You know,

894
54:46.621 --> 54:51.626
before I came here, I was a variety director for eight years.

895
54:52.327 --> 54:54.028
That's not the only reason I say this.

896
54:54.763 --> 54:58.633
But just as you approach sports with conviction,

897
54:59.200 --> 55:03.338
I know those guys pour their souls into making variety.

898
55:04.773 --> 55:09.010
Getting ratings is part of our job as TV people too.

899
55:10.078 --> 55:14.516
That's true for sports and variety alike.

900
55:15.617 --> 55:17.552
Nobody has the right

901
55:18.586 --> 55:21.423
to mock someone else's serious work.

902
55:29.264 --> 55:30.365
What's the show called?

903
55:32.434 --> 55:34.436
The one the Tamuken Pro pop idol quit.

904
55:35.637 --> 55:37.872
It's a late-night show called Laugh to Death.

905
55:43.311 --> 55:45.046
LAUGH TO DEATH

906
55:45.847 --> 55:48.016
Are you really okay with this, Mr. Watanabe?

907
55:48.082 --> 55:50.485
Hey, what about the foot-pressure rehearsal?

908
55:50.552 --> 55:51.619
Yes.

909
55:59.561 --> 56:01.396
Hey.

910
56:01.463 --> 56:02.564
Oh. Mr. Tokushige!

911
56:03.364 --> 56:05.200
-Long time no see. -Yeah.

912
56:06.568 --> 56:07.402
Well…

913
56:08.570 --> 56:09.537
I'm so sorry.

914
56:11.406 --> 56:13.475
I heard your cast member quit.

915
56:13.975 --> 56:17.645
I caused trouble for the show you started.

916
56:18.780 --> 56:20.081
I'm really sorry.

917
56:22.250 --> 56:25.854
If you like, I can find athletes

918
56:25.920 --> 56:27.755
who understand variety shows

919
56:27.822 --> 56:29.757
-for guest spots… -It's fine, Mr. Tokushige.

920
56:30.825 --> 56:32.894
-No, but… -Really, it's fine.

921
56:34.128 --> 56:35.997
If anything, I'm grateful.

922
56:37.031 --> 56:39.067
-Huh? -Actually,

923
56:39.133 --> 56:41.236
the Tamuken Pro pop idol who wanted out

924
56:41.803 --> 56:45.039
was brought in by Programming to boost the show.

925
56:47.642 --> 56:51.546
We launched Laugh to Death

926
56:51.613 --> 56:53.114
around comedians going all out.

927
56:53.181 --> 56:54.015
BRAINSTORMING MEETING

928
56:54.082 --> 56:56.951
So we're getting back to our roots.

929
56:57.752 --> 56:59.420
More importantly, Mr. Tokushige.

930
57:00.555 --> 57:04.492
I heard Bureau Chief Kuroishi is trying to change Hakone.

931
57:07.462 --> 57:10.798
Don't give an inch.

932
57:34.122 --> 57:36.524
-Ready, start! -Okay!

933
57:39.060 --> 57:40.261
Pick up the speed a little!

934
57:40.328 --> 57:43.531
No! This really hurts!

935
57:43.598 --> 57:45.066
You got this! Two more meters!

936
57:46.367 --> 57:48.603
Lowering your foot more will make it look more real!

937
57:48.670 --> 57:49.637
Keep it gritty.

938
57:50.204 --> 57:52.874
-Get the sweat. Sweat! -Sweat!

939
57:52.941 --> 57:54.008
A little tighter!

940
57:54.075 --> 57:56.578
-Yes! -A little more!

941
57:56.644 --> 57:59.948
LAUGH TO DEATH

942
58:01.649 --> 58:02.550
Um…

943
58:04.252 --> 58:05.086
Yes?

944
58:05.753 --> 58:07.789
I'm Miyamoto from the Sports Department.

945
58:07.855 --> 58:11.793
Miyamoto… From the Hakone Ekiden?

946
58:12.594 --> 58:13.828
Yes.

947
58:15.563 --> 58:16.598
What can I do for you?

948
58:18.399 --> 58:20.001
I came to ask you a favor.

949
58:25.039 --> 58:27.008
REGARDING TAMUKEN PRO

950
58:27.075 --> 58:28.009
RYO TOKUSHIGE

951
58:28.076 --> 58:29.143
WE APOLOGIZE

952
58:29.210 --> 58:30.111
FOR THE CASTING ISSUE.

953
58:48.029 --> 58:51.232
THE HAKONE EKIDEN BROADCAST HANDBOOK

954
58:52.767 --> 58:53.801
63RD EKIDEN

955
58:53.868 --> 58:54.969
EKIDEN BROADCAST HANDBOOK

956
59:12.387 --> 59:13.688
Mr. Tokushige, what are you doing?

957
59:16.491 --> 59:19.594
You know the saying. "When in trouble, turn to the handbook."

958
59:19.661 --> 59:20.695
BROADCAST HANDBOOK-MANUAL

959
59:20.762 --> 59:27.168
SHOWING RUNNER'S INFORMATION AND CAMERA POSITION

960
59:29.203 --> 59:30.638
Did you find the answer?

961
59:30.705 --> 59:35.543
It's not that easy.

962
59:38.746 --> 59:41.716
Seeing them all like this, there are so many.

963
59:43.117 --> 59:45.086
It's history. Truly.

964
59:50.091 --> 59:51.059
Oh, sorry.

965
59:52.060 --> 59:53.828
This is hilarious.

966
59:54.429 --> 59:57.031
Next, we wrap up briefly at center, then go back to Car Three.

967
59:57.098 --> 59:58.666
Hold the commercial!

968
59:58.733 --> 01:00:00.601
Mr. Tokushige, we should go to commercial.

969
01:00:00.668 --> 01:00:02.036
Is it that?

970
01:00:02.103 --> 01:00:04.472
That's from when Miyamoto directed Car Three.

971
01:00:04.539 --> 01:00:07.341
You two had this gap even back then.

972
01:00:07.408 --> 01:00:08.910
I think we should go now.

973
01:00:08.976 --> 01:00:10.478
I said we're waiting!

974
01:00:10.545 --> 01:00:13.081
Nishiwaki of Teikyo University has gradually improved his pace

975
01:00:13.147 --> 01:00:15.016
since the five-kilometer mark.

976
01:00:15.083 --> 01:00:17.852
But even if he passes the school ahead, it'll take about three minutes.

977
01:00:17.919 --> 01:00:19.854
We should go to commercial now.

978
01:00:19.921 --> 01:00:21.089
Go to commercial!

979
01:00:21.155 --> 01:00:22.790
Come on!

980
01:00:22.857 --> 01:00:24.926
Doesn't the broadcast director have any pride?

981
01:00:24.992 --> 01:00:28.396
No, it's not about pride. Commercials matter.

982
01:00:34.001 --> 01:00:34.869
Is everything okay…

983
01:00:34.936 --> 01:00:35.770
MANAGING DIR. OFFICE

984
01:00:35.837 --> 01:00:37.105
…with the Tamuken Pro issue?

985
01:00:37.705 --> 01:00:40.475
I'm pulling together where things stand across the company.

986
01:00:43.277 --> 01:00:45.880
What do you plan to do now?

987
01:00:48.149 --> 01:00:50.518
Tokushige will take full responsibility.

988
01:00:51.319 --> 01:00:52.386
Responsibility?

989
01:00:54.789 --> 01:00:59.594
I'll take him off Hakone.

990
01:01:01.095 --> 01:01:03.531
Hello, thank you as always.

991
01:01:03.598 --> 01:01:05.967
This is Tokushige from Dainichi TV.

992
01:01:07.101 --> 01:01:08.002
MEISEI GAKUIN UNIVERSITY

993
01:01:08.069 --> 01:01:09.003
TRACK AND FIELD DORMITORY

994
01:01:10.238 --> 01:01:11.305
Excuse me.

995
01:01:12.140 --> 01:01:12.974
What is it?

996
01:01:13.841 --> 01:01:17.178
Coach, could I talk to you about something?

997
01:01:24.285 --> 01:01:26.821
I heard about it.

998
01:01:27.955 --> 01:01:30.725
Tohto Chuo Bussan's community program.

999
01:01:31.759 --> 01:01:35.797
And that you'll only coach for one year.

1000
01:01:41.736 --> 01:01:42.703
But…

1001
01:01:43.671 --> 01:01:46.641
can you build a team that makes it to Hakone that way?

1002
01:01:48.476 --> 01:01:50.812
A lot of the team isn't convinced.

1003
01:01:55.650 --> 01:01:56.551
And you?

1004
01:01:57.652 --> 01:01:59.787
-Huh? -What do you think?

1005
01:02:04.058 --> 01:02:07.562
I think one year will be tough.

1006
01:02:10.097 --> 01:02:11.532
But right now,

1007
01:02:12.333 --> 01:02:15.636
I think the problem is that the team is divided.

1008
01:02:18.472 --> 01:02:21.142
I know that as captain,

1009
01:02:21.809 --> 01:02:26.113
I should be the one to pull us together, but…

1010
01:02:28.583 --> 01:02:31.452
"I cost us the qualifying race.

1011
01:02:31.519 --> 01:02:32.753
I don't have the confidence."

1012
01:02:34.956 --> 01:02:36.057
Is that it?

1013
01:02:42.597 --> 01:02:43.731
Yes.

1014
01:02:44.899 --> 01:02:46.100
It's because of me…

1015
01:02:48.436 --> 01:02:50.571
that our team didn't make Hakone.

1016
01:02:52.073 --> 01:02:55.843
And that's why you're unsure about running for the Student United Team.

1017
01:03:05.353 --> 01:03:06.320
Do I even

1018
01:03:08.222 --> 01:03:10.391
deserve to run Hakone?

1019
01:03:13.527 --> 01:03:18.399
Isn't resolve more important than whether you deserve it?

1020
01:03:19.433 --> 01:03:20.334
Huh?

1021
01:03:20.401 --> 01:03:22.370
If you turn it down,

1022
01:03:22.937 --> 01:03:25.706
what happens to the guys criticizing you now?

1023
01:03:29.277 --> 01:03:30.511
They'd be hurt, don't you think?

1024
01:03:32.146 --> 01:03:32.980
Hurt?

1025
01:03:33.047 --> 01:03:34.715
"He gave up

1026
01:03:35.583 --> 01:03:37.251
Hakone because of me."

1027
01:03:38.719 --> 01:03:40.554
Do you want them to regret that?

1028
01:03:43.291 --> 01:03:47.461
Anger is much easier than regret.

1029
01:03:51.032 --> 01:03:55.736
Next week, I'll gather the runners picked for the Student United Team

1030
01:03:56.337 --> 01:03:57.805
and begin team practice.

1031
01:04:04.946 --> 01:04:08.883
I'm staking my future

1032
01:04:08.950 --> 01:04:10.818
as a coach on this Hakone.

1033
01:04:12.353 --> 01:04:15.556
Aoba, make the team

1034
01:04:17.024 --> 01:04:18.793
accept you with your running.

1035
01:04:20.561 --> 01:04:23.497
Until then, don't listen to any of the noise.

1036
01:04:24.832 --> 01:04:26.434
I'll hear the complaints after Hakone.

1037
01:04:29.036 --> 01:04:30.004
How about it, Aoba?

1038
01:04:31.372 --> 01:04:32.239
Can you do it?

1039
01:04:36.644 --> 01:04:37.678
I can.

1040
01:04:39.280 --> 01:04:43.985
DAY OF EXECUTIVE MEETING

1041
01:04:49.557 --> 01:04:50.391
Yes.

1042
01:04:51.993 --> 01:04:52.927
Thank you for waiting.

1043
01:04:55.596 --> 01:04:56.630
Okay.

1044
01:05:01.168 --> 01:05:02.236
Will he be okay?

1045
01:05:02.303 --> 01:05:04.672
The executive meeting is soon, right?

1046
01:05:06.073 --> 01:05:08.109
He'll be fine. It's Mr. Tokushige.

1047
01:05:18.886 --> 01:05:19.754
Right this way.

1048
01:05:19.820 --> 01:05:20.654
EXECUTIVE ROOM

1049
01:05:26.694 --> 01:05:27.561
Please.

1050
01:05:38.539 --> 01:05:39.540
Have a seat.

1051
01:05:58.993 --> 01:06:00.361
DAINICHI TV PRESIDENT HIDEHIKO TAKESHIBA

1052
01:06:00.428 --> 01:06:02.897
Let's move to the last item on the agenda.

1053
01:06:02.963 --> 01:06:06.534
Our chief producer for the Hakone Ekiden, Tokushige,

1054
01:06:06.600 --> 01:06:09.470
will explain what happened.

1055
01:06:09.537 --> 01:06:12.106
Losing Tamuken Pro's trust is a major blow

1056
01:06:12.673 --> 01:06:15.976
to our drama and variety divisions.

1057
01:06:16.744 --> 01:06:19.880
It's already disrupted production of several programs.

1058
01:06:22.216 --> 01:06:23.451
Tokushige,

1059
01:06:24.385 --> 01:06:26.120
please explain how this came about.

1060
01:06:27.755 --> 01:06:28.756
Yes.

1061
01:06:34.061 --> 01:06:35.529
Before I do,

1062
01:06:36.097 --> 01:06:39.400
may I share something with everyone?

1063
01:06:39.467 --> 01:06:40.534
Is it okay?

1064
01:06:48.542 --> 01:06:52.780
This is what we call

1065
01:06:52.847 --> 01:06:54.381
the Hakone Ekiden Broadcast Handbook.

1066
01:06:54.982 --> 01:06:57.485
It contains everything,

1067
01:06:57.551 --> 01:07:00.187
from runner info to camera positions.

1068
01:07:00.254 --> 01:07:04.525
It's essentially a manual for broadcasting the Hakone Ekiden.

1069
01:07:04.592 --> 01:07:07.228
But that's not all.

1070
01:07:08.662 --> 01:07:10.564
It records our passion

1071
01:07:10.631 --> 01:07:12.099
for each year's broadcast.

1072
01:07:12.166 --> 01:07:16.504
It's an emotional anchor for us.

1073
01:07:16.570 --> 01:07:19.907
What does that have to do with today's agenda?

1074
01:07:22.209 --> 01:07:25.312
This is the very first

1075
01:07:25.846 --> 01:07:28.482
broadcast handbook.

1076
01:07:29.783 --> 01:07:30.985
Please look here.

1077
01:07:31.719 --> 01:07:33.621
63RD

1078
01:07:33.687 --> 01:07:35.723
It says "63rd."

1079
01:07:35.789 --> 01:07:37.057
Yes.

1080
01:07:37.758 --> 01:07:39.527
Why does our first broadcast

1081
01:07:40.060 --> 01:07:42.163
say 63rd?

1082
01:07:43.097 --> 01:07:46.867
Because we only started

1083
01:07:47.401 --> 01:07:50.437
broadcasting from the 63rd race.

1084
01:07:50.504 --> 01:07:51.405
I asked

1085
01:07:52.640 --> 01:07:56.010
what this has to do with today's meeting!

1086
01:07:57.878 --> 01:08:00.281
The first race

1087
01:08:00.347 --> 01:08:02.616
was held in 1920.

1088
01:08:03.284 --> 01:08:07.288
It's gone on for over a century.

1089
01:08:08.322 --> 01:08:11.492
Over its long history,

1090
01:08:11.559 --> 01:08:15.062
the Hakone Ekiden was halted by war.

1091
01:08:16.397 --> 01:08:17.498
But even then,

1092
01:08:18.432 --> 01:08:20.568
the runners wanted to run

1093
01:08:21.135 --> 01:08:22.903
through the ruins of Tokyo again.

1094
01:08:23.537 --> 01:08:25.105
They wanted to pass the sash.

1095
01:08:26.307 --> 01:08:27.908
They never gave up running.

1096
01:08:29.777 --> 01:08:33.647
The Hakone Ekiden was started by runners

1097
01:08:33.714 --> 01:08:36.750
and kept alive by runners.

1098
01:08:37.851 --> 01:08:40.020
Our job as a TV station

1099
01:08:40.087 --> 01:08:42.723
is to show their race as it truly is.

1100
01:08:42.790 --> 01:08:46.360
Exactly as it happens.

1101
01:08:47.161 --> 01:08:48.596
Nothing more.

1102
01:08:56.971 --> 01:08:57.871
Hey.

1103
01:08:58.973 --> 01:09:00.241
Enough already.

1104
01:09:01.175 --> 01:09:03.077
That's not what I'm asking.

1105
01:09:03.644 --> 01:09:05.779
Your reckless actions have already disrupted

1106
01:09:05.846 --> 01:09:07.648
our programming.

1107
01:09:07.715 --> 01:09:09.883
How will you take responsibility?

1108
01:09:09.950 --> 01:09:11.252
That's what I'm asking!

1109
01:09:11.318 --> 01:09:13.254
Do you understand

1110
01:09:13.320 --> 01:09:14.755
how serious your mistake is?

1111
01:09:18.058 --> 01:09:20.427
I'm the chief producer of the Hakone Ekiden.

1112
01:09:20.494 --> 01:09:21.428
So what?

1113
01:09:22.162 --> 01:09:22.997
As you say,

1114
01:09:23.731 --> 01:09:25.666
all responsibility lies with me.

1115
01:09:26.533 --> 01:09:27.801
But that also means

1116
01:09:27.868 --> 01:09:31.138
the authority to decide the broadcast

1117
01:09:31.205 --> 01:09:32.506
should be mine.

1118
01:09:34.308 --> 01:09:38.078
Sir, he's trying to change the subject.

1119
01:09:38.145 --> 01:09:39.446
The problem is…

1120
01:09:40.681 --> 01:09:42.516
his reckless actions

1121
01:09:43.050 --> 01:09:46.353
have caused major losses.

1122
01:09:47.921 --> 01:09:49.156
Bureau Chief Kuroishi.

1123
01:09:49.823 --> 01:09:52.960
This isn't just me acting on my own.

1124
01:09:53.994 --> 01:09:54.995
What do you mean?

1125
01:09:56.997 --> 01:10:02.903
Actually, our sponsor, Miyako Beer made a request the other day.

1126
01:10:03.570 --> 01:10:04.872
Miyako Beer did?

1127
01:10:04.938 --> 01:10:06.473
Miyako Beer did?

1128
01:10:07.041 --> 01:10:08.509
What is it?

1129
01:10:08.575 --> 01:10:12.012
They can't support a format

1130
01:10:12.079 --> 01:10:15.716
that casts celebrities.

1131
01:10:17.651 --> 01:10:20.621
-Miyako Beer said that? -Really?

1132
01:10:20.688 --> 01:10:22.222
What a bluff.

1133
01:10:23.557 --> 01:10:24.725
It's not a bluff.

1134
01:10:25.726 --> 01:10:26.860
Fine.

1135
01:10:26.927 --> 01:10:28.529
I'll check with Miyako Beer myself.

1136
01:10:29.096 --> 01:10:31.765
There's no need.

1137
01:10:37.504 --> 01:10:39.873
Sorry to keep you waiting. I'll put you through now.

1138
01:10:41.342 --> 01:10:42.910
-Excuse me. -Yes.

1139
01:10:44.178 --> 01:10:47.214
Could you put this on that monitor?

1140
01:10:47.781 --> 01:10:49.383
I'm connected with Miyako Beer.

1141
01:10:49.450 --> 01:10:50.284
Huh?

1142
01:11:00.294 --> 01:11:01.128
Put it through.

1143
01:11:02.196 --> 01:11:03.163
Thank you.

1144
01:11:08.068 --> 01:11:09.169
It's connected.

1145
01:11:13.040 --> 01:11:15.743
This is Mr. Sone, sales director at Miyako Beer.

1146
01:11:17.778 --> 01:11:20.214
Mr. Sone, please take it from here.

1147
01:11:20.914 --> 01:11:23.117
My apologies for interrupting

1148
01:11:23.183 --> 01:11:25.919
your important executive meeting.

1149
01:11:27.121 --> 01:11:30.457
I asked for your valuable time today

1150
01:11:30.524 --> 01:11:34.128
to restate our basic sponsorship policy.

1151
01:11:34.695 --> 01:11:37.197
At Miyako Beer,

1152
01:11:37.798 --> 01:11:38.866
we want the Hakone Ekiden

1153
01:11:40.300 --> 01:11:43.404
broadcast in its usual format.

1154
01:11:44.738 --> 01:11:46.507
Unfortunately,

1155
01:11:46.573 --> 01:11:49.276
we can't agree to changes such as bringing in

1156
01:11:49.343 --> 01:11:51.812
celebrities as guests or hosts.

1157
01:11:53.981 --> 01:11:55.249
Hello.

1158
01:11:55.783 --> 01:11:57.551
I'm Managing Director Kashiwagi.

1159
01:11:58.118 --> 01:11:59.019
Mr. Sone.

1160
01:12:00.053 --> 01:12:03.056
Is that your company's official position?

1161
01:12:04.258 --> 01:12:05.259
Of course.

1162
01:12:06.427 --> 01:12:08.896
You may take it as our company's consensus.

1163
01:12:10.731 --> 01:12:12.499
We take pride

1164
01:12:12.566 --> 01:12:14.468
in having run alongside

1165
01:12:14.535 --> 01:12:17.704
this broadcast since the first one.

1166
01:12:19.206 --> 01:12:23.210
We hope Dainichi TV will keep airing the proud,

1167
01:12:23.277 --> 01:12:25.512
passionate Hakone Ekiden.

1168
01:12:26.713 --> 01:12:28.649
That is Miyako Beer's wish.

1169
01:12:30.651 --> 01:12:33.887
Thank you for your consideration.

1170
01:12:39.660 --> 01:12:42.296
Thank you, Mr. Sone.

1171
01:12:42.863 --> 01:12:43.864
Mr. Tokushige,

1172
01:12:44.932 --> 01:12:46.934
I'm looking forward to the next Hakone.

1173
01:12:49.503 --> 01:12:52.105
Goodbye.

1174
01:12:57.644 --> 01:12:59.413
As you just saw,

1175
01:13:00.247 --> 01:13:03.350
it's not just the runners and staff.

1176
01:13:04.485 --> 01:13:06.220
The sponsors are passionate too.

1177
01:13:07.488 --> 01:13:11.024
That's the Hakone Ekiden.

1178
01:13:16.797 --> 01:13:19.132
I see. That's enough.

1179
01:13:19.199 --> 01:13:23.103
Programming jumped the gun this time.

1180
01:13:24.805 --> 01:13:27.674
Wasn't there a lack of communication with the staff?

1181
01:13:30.244 --> 01:13:35.516
Once President Tamura agrees to appear,

1182
01:13:35.582 --> 01:13:37.784
he won't back down quietly.

1183
01:13:39.286 --> 01:13:42.923
We need to stay on good terms with Tamuken Pro.

1184
01:13:44.258 --> 01:13:46.260
So, Kuroishi,

1185
01:13:48.996 --> 01:13:52.966
cleaning up this mess is on you.

1186
01:13:53.700 --> 01:13:54.535
Understood?

1187
01:13:57.371 --> 01:13:58.705
Understood.

1188
01:14:02.409 --> 01:14:03.377
Good work.

1189
01:14:04.211 --> 01:14:07.814
Keep it up and make it a great broadcast worthy of Hakone.

1190
01:14:10.584 --> 01:14:11.451
Yes!

1191
01:14:16.089 --> 01:14:16.924
-Huh? -Huh?

1192
01:14:16.990 --> 01:14:17.991
Really?

1193
01:14:18.992 --> 01:14:20.394
‎At the executive meeting,

1194
01:14:23.263 --> 01:14:26.066
‎they gave the green light

1195
01:14:26.567 --> 01:14:28.268
‎for a great Hakone broadcast.

1196
01:14:28.335 --> 01:14:30.871
So don't worry

1197
01:14:30.938 --> 01:14:32.906
and get back to work!

1198
01:14:33.707 --> 01:14:35.442
-Yeah! -Thank goodness!

1199
01:14:36.476 --> 01:14:40.314
Yeah!

1200
01:14:41.448 --> 01:14:43.016
Yeah!

1201
01:14:48.956 --> 01:14:51.592
-Cheers! -Cheers!

1202
01:14:54.494 --> 01:14:57.130
I'm so glad!

1203
01:14:57.197 --> 01:14:59.800
I was sure you were going to be transferred.

1204
01:14:59.866 --> 01:15:01.902
Don't say that so casually.

1205
01:15:01.969 --> 01:15:04.504
I didn't know you knew someone at Miyako Beer.

1206
01:15:05.706 --> 01:15:07.574
You mean Mr. Sone, the sales director?

1207
01:15:07.641 --> 01:15:11.144
He ran track all through school.

1208
01:15:11.211 --> 01:15:13.580
Hakone means a lot to him.

1209
01:15:14.214 --> 01:15:15.115
He'd get fired up about it when drunk.

1210
01:15:15.182 --> 01:15:17.451
I was surprised Miyako Beer backed us so completely.

1211
01:15:17.517 --> 01:15:20.487
They haven't been Hakone's main sponsor

1212
01:15:20.554 --> 01:15:24.091
for nearly 40 years for nothing.

1213
01:15:24.157 --> 01:15:25.859
Right.

1214
01:15:25.926 --> 01:15:29.196
So many people have kept Hakone going.

1215
01:15:29.262 --> 01:15:31.264
Oh, a rare good line from you.

1216
01:15:31.331 --> 01:15:32.699
What do you mean, rare?

1217
01:15:32.766 --> 01:15:36.203
Didn't you want Mr. Hatakeyama on?

1218
01:15:37.471 --> 01:15:40.140
Now, now. Have a drink.

1219
01:15:40.207 --> 01:15:42.609
But isn't it great?

1220
01:15:42.676 --> 01:15:44.811
At least we avoided a crazy variety makeover.

1221
01:15:46.146 --> 01:15:47.514
Yeah.

1222
01:15:47.581 --> 01:15:51.618
But changing with the times is one option too.

1223
01:15:53.553 --> 01:15:55.188
By the way, did you all know?

1224
01:15:55.255 --> 01:15:57.924
Natsuki's hooked on variety shows lately.

1225
01:15:57.991 --> 01:16:00.027
-Hey. -You've been watching

1226
01:16:00.093 --> 01:16:01.895
all the old episodes of Laugh to Death, right?

1227
01:16:01.962 --> 01:16:03.330
What?

1228
01:16:03.397 --> 01:16:04.898
That's an edgy pick.

1229
01:16:04.965 --> 01:16:07.501
-So? How was it? -Huh?

1230
01:16:07.567 --> 01:16:09.102
What do you think of it?

1231
01:16:13.073 --> 01:16:14.141
It's not funny at all.

1232
01:16:15.976 --> 01:16:17.978
Actually, I don't really know

1233
01:16:18.045 --> 01:16:20.047
where I'm supposed to laugh.

1234
01:16:20.113 --> 01:16:21.314
So I'm analyzing it.

1235
01:16:21.381 --> 01:16:22.983
-Analyzing? -Yes.

1236
01:16:23.050 --> 01:16:25.652
Last night was the "Layered Underwear Championship."

1237
01:16:25.719 --> 01:16:27.154
Why wear layers of underwear?

1238
01:16:27.220 --> 01:16:30.691
And why is it funny when you wear layers of underwear?

1239
01:16:30.757 --> 01:16:32.626
Aren't you overdoing it a bit?

1240
01:16:32.693 --> 01:16:34.027
Forget the underwear.

1241
01:16:34.094 --> 01:16:36.697
I'd rather you focus completely on Hakone right now.

1242
01:16:36.763 --> 01:16:37.798
Of course.

1243
01:16:42.869 --> 01:16:45.272
Now it sounds like I said something strange.

1244
01:16:47.741 --> 01:16:49.676
TOHO UNIVERSITY OF ECONOMICS STUDENT UNITED TEAM

1245
01:16:49.743 --> 01:16:51.111
MEETING DAY

1246
01:16:51.178 --> 01:16:52.112
TOHO UNIVERSITY OF ECONOMICS TRACK AND FIELD TEAM

1247
01:16:52.179 --> 01:16:55.382
What is the purpose of this Student United Team?

1248
01:16:55.982 --> 01:16:59.086
We first need to make that clear.

1249
01:17:02.155 --> 01:17:03.657
My goal is a top-three finish

1250
01:17:04.858 --> 01:17:06.660
at the Hakone Ekiden.

1251
01:18:30.844 --> 01:18:32.078
‎I'm the only one who can go.

1252
01:18:32.145 --> 01:18:33.847
‎56 DAYS UNTIL HAKONE EKIDEN

1253
01:18:33.914 --> 01:18:35.015
‎THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION ‎BASED ON THE HAKONE EKIDEN.

1254
01:18:35.081 --> 01:18:36.082
‎ALL PEOPLE AND ORGANIZATIONS DEPICTED ‎ARE UNRELATED TO REAL ONES.

1255
01:18:36.149 --> 01:18:37.083
‎STUDENT ACTIVITIES AND RULES IN THIS DRAMA ‎ARE FICTIONAL AND DON'T REFLECT REALITY.

1256
